{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>You shall place in the mouth of the youngest's sack.</b> What Yosef placed on Binyamin was a pretext, because he did not recognize him — since they had left him without the growth of a beard, he said in his heart: perhaps they brought me a foundling from the marketplace. He said: I will frame him with a pretext — if he is their brother, they will not abandon him."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 44, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:08:32.040410853Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}